00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:05.020
Episode Twenty-Five: 
Goodbye

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:17.610
Twelve minutes until the investigation group reaches the Fracture.

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:22.350
3 hours, 51 minutes until the Fracture reaches the final defense line.

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:25.500
If we are unable to stop it, then in four hours...

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:27.900
...we will be swallowed up by the Fracture.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:30.560
It will be the end of the Sol system.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:34.550
To be entrusted with the final stronghold at my age...

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:37.970
If it were possible, I'd rather just be an onlooker...

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:39.820
...watching the course of events at they unfold.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:40.970
Right...

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:43.870
There are no changes to the mission.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:51.980
Gather as much data as you can on the minimum point...

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:53.060
...and send it to the Halcyon.

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:57.110
Be sure to pay enough attention to your distance from the Fracture.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.520
If you touch it, your molecules will be scattered...

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:08.270
In surfing, it would be the ideal wave.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:10.320
Have you ever surfed?
 No.

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:16.050
Oh!

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:17.060
Whoa!

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:19.350
All right, then.

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:23.970
With this, we can understand the situation.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.020
Did you hack into the mission system?

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:28.890
It's the path that Shipon made during the study session...

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:31.230
...when she accessed the computer without permission.

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:37.300
Be careful of the gravity barrier's output!

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:39.600
If we lose our balance by even one point...

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:40.790
...the whole thing will be thrown off.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:42.890
We won't make any blunders like that!

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:44.870
I just might...

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:51.210
If we do it following this procedure...

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:53.270
...then even I'll be able to install it.

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:56.740
Analysis complete.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:58.700
It appears that the El Santo's collapse was caused...

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:01.510
...by the current of the Fracture's gravitational field.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:03.160
Predictions for outbreaks?

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:04.510
They're irregular.

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:06.020
We cannot make any predictions.

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:07.450
This is a problem.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:09.520
What about the Halcyon?

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:12.240
Operational rate is at 60%.

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:14.660
The adjustments will take a little more time.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:16.130
That's fine.

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:18.050
We still have time.

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:39.970
The investigation group has reached the mission area!

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:42.280
Begin your investigation of the minimum point.

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:43.410
Roger!

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:45.600
All right, let's go!

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:46.560
Roger!
Understood.

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:57.750
3 hours, 19 minutes until the Fracture reaches the absolute defense line.

00:04:58.360 --> 00:04:59.750
Begin supplying electrical power.

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:03.620
Supplying cannons with electrical power!

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:09.110
Beam cannons numbers one to three are at critical levels.

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:11.810
Number four and number five are at critical levels.

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:14.750
Releasing all generators.

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:32.470
Gravity lens formation complete!

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:34.300
Perform final check on the alignment.

00:05:34.610 --> 00:05:36.640
Alignment on cannons one to three is fine.

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:38.410
Alignment on four to five is fine.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:40.210
The alignment on the gravity lens is set!

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:43.550
2,000 meters in front of the Infinity...

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:48.530
1,000 meters... 500... 400...

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:51.450
300... 200...

00:05:56.280 --> 00:06:01.400
"Present fears are less than horrible imaginings." From Macbeth.

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:07.960
That's it!

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:14.000
All right! Mark!

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:19.420
Difficult, isn't it?

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:21.900
A gravitational displacement?

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:24.700
It's a gravitational field current!

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:29.620
Escape while we can!

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:42.980
How much longer?

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:44.450
About 60 minutes.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.940
The Fracture has just passed the three hour mark.

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:50.520
When the assault begins, the Fracture will slow down.

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:52.930
This won't end with us as bystanders!

00:06:56.860 --> 00:06:58.070
It's no use! Dodge it!

00:06:58.070 --> 00:06:58.830
Here it comes!

00:06:58.900 --> 00:07:00.360
It's no good! I can't control it!

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:02.420
Don't worry about it! Mark the minimum point!

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:03.730
I can't read its movements!

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:05.830
Damn it to hell!

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:10.010
It's no good... At this rate, there will just be more victims...

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:13.050
I have to... I have to do it...

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:16.380
There are too many gravitational field currents!

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:17.420
What's going on?!

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:20.310
We've gone too far ahead! Go back! Go back!

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:21.680
Is the Halcyon still not ready yet?!

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:22.510
Where's the Halcyon?!

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:24.040
Where's the Halcyon?!

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:27.280
The number of ships that can continue has been reduced to 70%!

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:30.690
The rate of gravitational field current occurrences is rising!

00:07:31.240 --> 00:07:33.440
We believe that they are being incited...

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:34.650
...by the Ora-avis machines' gravity control systems!

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:38.060
Hurry up with the damage assessment!

00:07:44.010 --> 00:07:46.220
Damn it! It's too fast, I can't mark it!

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:48.560
It feels like we're going to be swallowed up by the Fracture!

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:51.080
Where's the minimum point? Concentrate...

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:55.010
Concentrate on the Vision!

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:58.770
I... I have to do it...

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:16.540
D-Don't get in my way!

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:19.570
You mustn't be impatient! You mustn't be impatient!

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:23.170
I'm not being impatient! I've got to do it!

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:26.620
I'm the one that can use the DLS the best!

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:29.100
Yeah, you're right.

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:32.340
But you need to concentrate on the firing control.

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:34.130
You can only fire twice, after all.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:38.410
Processing the information is my duty. I'll do my best...

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:53.940
I'm sorry I'm late.

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:01.010
The Halcyon's system adjustments are complete!

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:02.210
All right!

00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:10.530
This is the Halcyon. Preparations for data reception are complete.

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:12.910
It's all right even if you don't mark it.

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:14.790
Please get me confirmation information...

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:16.290
Even a little bit more counts.

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:19.820
I'll process it here and take hold of it!

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:23.470
Take hold of it, hmm?

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:25.440
In that case, we need to reestablish our positions!

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:38.500
It's all right...

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:41.250
The system is functioning at 100%...

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:49.750
Huh?

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:51.590
Hmm? What's wrong?

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:52.320
Well...

00:09:53.970 --> 00:09:57.210
2 hours, 38 minutes until the Fracture reaches the absolute defense line!

00:09:58.840 --> 00:09:59.780
Relax...

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:03.070
Relax...

00:10:19.710 --> 00:10:21.440
Something seems different...

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:22.430
What is it?

00:10:22.670 --> 00:10:25.260
Something is...

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:30.350
Kouta!

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:32.670
I see it!

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:35.550
The Infinity has locked onto the minimum point!

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:37.900
All units in the investigation group...

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:41.080
...go to the defense of the Infinity and the Halcyon!

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:43.770
The rest is up to you!

00:10:44.430 --> 00:10:44.720
Right!

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:55.860
Launch the Odyssey!

00:11:09.470 --> 00:11:10.110
Odyssey...

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:23.640
When the Fracture's movements slow, I'll do the final corrections...

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:26.820
When it slows, I'll do the final corrections...

00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:37.670
The Odyssey is going in!

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:41.690
Damn it...

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:05.110
I can't see it, but the Fracture's movements have just slowed...

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:10.430
Don't lose your head, and relax...

00:12:26.450 --> 00:12:27.140
All right!

00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:28.850
Data correction is complete!

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:30.410
Revise focal distance!

00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:32.200
Revising focal distance!

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:47.070
Energy charging complete!

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:53.570
Fire!

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:19.080
What?!

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:25.760
The beam curved?!

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:27.900
What's going on?

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:30.210
It's because of the gravitational field currents!

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:33.250
It appears that the beam was pulled towards...

00:13:40.220 --> 00:13:41.340
It missed...

00:13:43.600 --> 00:13:46.000
It's just like... it's alive...

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:48.310
So it reacted to the beam?

00:13:48.770 --> 00:13:52.270
If we can't deal with the gravitational field, then this mission is...

00:14:02.890 --> 00:14:03.670
It's no use...

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:18.300
I won't let it lay a single finger on either of you!

00:14:20.240 --> 00:14:22.000
Let all the ships assigned to this mission...

00:14:22.070 --> 00:14:23.040
...retreat to the second offense area!

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:25.540
Prepare to fire the second shot!

00:14:33.130 --> 00:14:33.800
Katase?

00:14:34.230 --> 00:14:35.710
Y-Yes, sir! I'm doing it...

00:14:36.780 --> 00:14:38.740
But there's so little data...

00:14:39.320 --> 00:14:41.610
It's all right. We can still fire two more shots.

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:43.950
We'll use the next shot to gather data...

00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:46.750
...so finish the program to predict the current.

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:49.330
We just have to get it with the third shot.

00:14:49.590 --> 00:14:52.910
But the only Foundation we can hit it with is the Akapusu!

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:55.170
There's still the Stellvia...

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:09.160
With the loss of the El Santo, the mission has sped up.

00:15:09.940 --> 00:15:12.200
But beyond that, everything else is going as planned.

00:15:13.060 --> 00:15:16.080
I want you to use the abilities you possess to their full extent.

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:29.170
Releasing the generators into a new orbit. Beginning movement.

00:15:30.100 --> 00:15:31.860
Linking communications to the Stellvia.

00:15:32.270 --> 00:15:34.260
Transferring the control of the generators to the Stellvia.

00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:35.850
How is it?

00:15:36.520 --> 00:15:38.630
It's an older model, but it's more than useable.

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:40.710
But no matter how hard we try...

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:42.650
...it's still a generator used to gather resources.

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:45.770
It can only be used as a replacement for the Stellvia once.

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:47.130
That's enough!

00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:52.250
It feels like he said that he believes in the potential.

00:15:55.660 --> 00:15:58.640
From here on, they're going to go and make history.

00:15:59.910 --> 00:16:04.340
Being able to continue to carry hope will lead them to strength.

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:07.320
That's right...

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:09.370
It's as you say.

00:16:11.750 --> 00:16:14.720
2 hours, 22 minutes until it reaches the absolute defense line!

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:20.990
With this one shot...

00:16:22.320 --> 00:16:23.940
...a miss is absolutely not an option.

00:16:24.800 --> 00:16:26.920
If it misses, then the Stellvia will be...

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:32.130
There are still two shots...

00:16:33.540 --> 00:16:34.350
Still two...

00:16:37.790 --> 00:16:41.080
Hmm... Something really does seem different...

00:16:41.550 --> 00:16:42.710
So what is it?

00:16:43.320 --> 00:16:44.820
Hmm...

00:16:45.570 --> 00:16:48.900
I was wondering if Shipon's program was like this...

00:16:50.060 --> 00:16:52.480
The Infinity has locked on to the minimum point!

00:16:54.250 --> 00:16:55.560
Launch the Akapusu!

00:17:06.910 --> 00:17:09.130
They say we can still fire two more times...

00:17:09.310 --> 00:17:11.370
...but I don't intend on wasting this shot!

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:14.600
If we're going to settle it, then let's settle it with this one!

00:17:14.980 --> 00:17:15.530
Okay...

00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:18.860
I have to increase the frequency of the operations, even if only a little...

00:17:20.090 --> 00:17:21.690
I have to improve our chance...

00:17:22.850 --> 00:17:25.410
Do it... Do it...

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:31.260
The Akapusu is going in!

00:17:43.320 --> 00:17:44.640
Data correction complete!

00:17:45.020 --> 00:17:46.540
Revise focal distance! Prepare to fire!

00:17:58.500 --> 00:17:59.290
Fire!

00:18:09.430 --> 00:18:10.930
Even if a gravitational field current comes at us...

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:20.140
That was close!

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:21.000
Yes!

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:35.460
It's going to be the Stellvia's turn soon.

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:38.140
Our Stellvia's...

00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:41.290
That's why we need to settle it with the third shot.

00:18:41.610 --> 00:18:43.330
Shipon will be able to take hold of it.

00:18:43.520 --> 00:18:44.010
Yeah.

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:47.370
If we can increase the Halcyon's output with this generator, then...

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:52.080
How is it, Katase?

00:18:52.430 --> 00:18:53.410
Y-Yes, sir!

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:56.710
I was able to collect the data on the gravitational field's currents.

00:18:57.400 --> 00:18:59.950
I'm going to begin revising the program.

00:19:00.580 --> 00:19:03.620
We're going to pull the mission area back to the final defense line.

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:06.020
We'll be able to earn some more time, too.

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:07.500
Relax, then get to it.

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:08.220
Yes, sir...

00:19:12.930 --> 00:19:14.610
Attention, all hands.

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:18.020
From here on, we're going to move the Stellvia into the mission area.

00:19:19.150 --> 00:19:21.290
All personnel, evacuate in a quick and orderly fashion.

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:24.580
We're going to transfer the control functions to the Vision.

00:19:25.840 --> 00:19:28.030
Stellvia, move out!

00:19:38.260 --> 00:19:41.360
Begin reverse propulsion from C1 to 5.

00:19:41.760 --> 00:19:45.490
Please report status on the generators in blocks B and D.

00:19:46.130 --> 00:19:48.330
Working while I sit doesn't suit me.

00:19:49.050 --> 00:19:50.930
You were originally a pilot, after all.

00:19:51.390 --> 00:19:53.560
It's just that I'm used to standing around and talking.

00:19:55.730 --> 00:19:59.280
I'm going to go to the mission area as I am and take command.

00:19:59.810 --> 00:20:01.600
Don't worry about the cannons.

00:20:10.880 --> 00:20:12.980
Everything is up to my program...

00:20:13.760 --> 00:20:14.840
I have to hurry...

00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:16.090
I have to hurry...

00:20:39.820 --> 00:20:41.270
Can you hear me, Shipon?

00:20:42.750 --> 00:20:43.520
Dai-chan?

00:20:45.420 --> 00:20:46.130
Hold on!

00:20:46.660 --> 00:20:48.440
After all that, even the Stellvia will be sacrificed...

00:20:49.690 --> 00:20:52.980
If I did... If I just did it right...

00:20:53.530 --> 00:20:54.260
Kouta!

00:20:56.310 --> 00:20:58.160
There's a gravitational shift in the mission area!

00:20:58.300 --> 00:20:58.850
What?!

00:20:59.260 --> 00:20:59.780
A huge one!

00:21:03.420 --> 00:21:04.670
All units, evacuate!

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:14.210
What the...?

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:20.310
What's wrong, Otoyama?

00:21:20.600 --> 00:21:22.120
I can't increase the output!

00:21:23.320 --> 00:21:26.030
Damn it! Is this because of the load factor from when it was fired?

00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:33.810
Gravity barrier, full power!

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:50.500
Shi...!

00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:53.970
Shima-chan!

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:01.050
kono sora no iku hate ni

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:01.050
Where the end of this sky goes

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:01.050
この空の行く果てに

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:10.970
mada mienu mirai no nami ga ri

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:10.970
Are waves of the future that cannot yet be seen

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:10.970
まだ見えぬ 未来の波があり

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:21.010
ikite iru ikutsu mono unmei o koete yuku

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:21.010
We are alive; we overcome many destinies

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:21.010
生きている いくつもの運命を越えて行く

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:28.780
dare ni osowari dare ni koute iru no darou

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:28.780
Who are we learning from, who are we asking?

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:28.780
誰に教わり 誰に請うているのだろう

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:37.600
hito wa tsukiru inochi no aima ni

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:37.600
People do not have time to fear encountering

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:37.600
人は尽きる命の合間に

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:46.570
deau koto ni obieru ma wa nai

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:46.570
The space between expiring lives

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:46.570
出会うことに 怯える間はない

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:57.240
tatoe kyou de kono sekai ga owarou to shite ite mo

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:57.240
Even if this world would end today

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:57.240
たとえ今日で この世界が終わろうとしていても

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:02.820
kimi o ai suru darou

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:02.820
I will still love you

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:02.820
君を愛するだろう

00:23:05.020 --> 00:23:07.030
Next Episode 

00:23:05.510 --> 00:23:06.430
Our first meeting was, that's right...

00:23:06.980 --> 00:23:08.800
...at the seats that were next to each other on the Fujiyama.

00:23:09.700 --> 00:23:13.810
When I saw how you were, before I knew it, I was concerned about you.

00:23:14.810 --> 00:23:16.060
You, who spoke of your dream.

00:23:16.810 --> 00:23:19.270
You, who were shy and lonely.

00:23:20.260 --> 00:23:23.030
You, who despite that, care for others indiscriminately.

00:23:23.980 --> 00:23:24.970
They are all you.

00:23:26.070 --> 00:23:27.630
The reason I spoke to you was...

00:23:28.200 --> 00:23:30.190
...because those things made you so much like her...

00:23:31.320 --> 00:23:33.170
On the next episode of Stellvia of the Universe...

00:23:32.050 --> 00:23:35.050
Episode Twenty-Six: 
Shining Voice "Shining Voice."

00:23:33.720 --> 00:23:34.700
Shining Voice 
